WEBVTT

1
00:00:12.267 --> 00:00:18.580
"Are you sure about this?" Maggie whispered.

2
00:00:18.581 --> 00:00:24.376
Henry didn't answer. He, Cole, and Maggie were crouched in an empty stall.

3
00:00:24.377 --> 00:00:29.075
They were watching the cat toy, which was lying in the aisle.

4
00:00:29.076 --> 00:00:33.389
"Shh," Henry whispered. "Someone's coming."

5
00:00:33.390 --> 00:00:38.552
Jill came into view. She spotted the cat toy and stopped.

6
00:00:38.553 --> 00:00:42.834
She looked up and down the aisle, and then leaned over to pick it up.

7
00:00:42.835 --> 00:00:47.179
Henry held his breath. Was his theory wrong?

8
00:00:47.180 --> 00:00:51.534
Jill straightened up again, dropping the cat toy back on the ground.

9
00:00:51.535 --> 00:00:57.361
"I don't get paid enough to pick up after messy riders," she muttered to herself.

10
00:00:57.362 --> 00:01:04.237
Henry let out his breath as she hurried away. So far his plan was going okay.

11
00:01:04.238 --> 00:01:08.221
He heard a bark as Little Spot trotted into sight.

12
00:01:08.222 --> 00:01:13.589
The dog paused to sniff the cat toy before lifting his head to look around the barn.

13
00:01:13.590 --> 00:01:16.067
Henry held his breath again.

14
00:01:16.068 --> 00:01:20.121
Was the dog going to walk away from the cat toy too?

15
00:01:20.122 --> 00:01:25.363
But Little Spot finally lowered his head, grabbed the toy, and took off.

16
00:01:25.364 --> 00:01:30.462
"Hurry!" Henry exclaimed. "We have to follow him!"

17
00:01:30.463 --> 00:01:35.888
He ran after Little Spot. Maggie and Cole were right behind him.

18
00:01:35.889 --> 00:01:39.499
The dog ran through the barn and out a side door.

19
00:01:39.500 --> 00:01:43.666
He crossed a courtyard and ran into another building.

20
00:01:43.667 --> 00:01:48.336
"He's headed for the hay shed!" Maggie said.

21
00:01:48.337 --> 00:01:52.788
Inside the shed, hay bales were stacked halfway to the ceiling.

22
00:01:52.789 --> 00:01:56.778
At first Henry couldn't see where Little Spot had gone.

23
00:01:56.779 --> 00:01:59.490
Then he heard a muffled bark.

24
00:01:59.491 --> 00:02:02.755
"This way!" Cole rushed around the bales.

25
00:02:02.756 --> 00:02:07.167
They found Little Spot in a narrow space behind the hay.

26
00:02:07.168 --> 00:02:11.313
He was wagging his tail and sitting on a dusty saddle pad.

27
00:02:11.314 --> 00:02:15.425
"Big Spot's saddle pad!" Maggie cried.

28
00:02:15.426 --> 00:02:19.555
"And look! The rest of my missing stuff is here too!"

29
00:02:19.556 --> 00:02:24.337
She grabbed her charm bracelet and slipped it on, and then picked up the cat toy.

30
00:02:24.338 --> 00:02:30.550
Next she dug through the hay until she found her brush, gloves, sock, and sandal.

31
00:02:30.551 --> 00:02:36.508
She even found the lost check. It was crumpled and had a few teeth holes in it.

32
00:02:36.509 --> 00:02:41.637
"I'll go tell Ms. Wood we solved the crime," Cole offered, hurrying back out.

33
00:02:41.638 --> 00:02:44.550
Henry spotted something else in the hay.

34
00:02:44.551 --> 00:02:49.237
"Look, Spot must have stolen this stuff too."

35
00:02:49.238 --> 00:02:53.894
"That looks like one of Ms. Wood's spare halters," Maggie said.

36
00:02:53.895 --> 00:02:56.747
"And here's another grooming brush!"

37
00:02:56.748 --> 00:03:00.420
Soon Ms. Wood arrived, along with Eleanor.

38
00:03:00.421 --> 00:03:06.250
"Little Spot!" Eleanor exclaimed, grabbing her dog and hugging him.

39
00:03:06.251 --> 00:03:11.312
"You rotten little thief! I'm really sorry, you guys.

40
00:03:11.313 --> 00:03:17.033
He does this at home sometimes, but I never thought he'd do it here.

41
00:03:17.034 --> 00:03:21.121
Usually he only steals stuff that smells like cats.

42
00:03:21.122 --> 00:03:24.308
For some reason he loves cats!"

43
00:03:24.309 --> 00:03:30.402
Henry grinned. "Yeah, we just figured that out," he said.

44
00:03:30.403 --> 00:03:33.509
"I saw him licking the barn cat.

45
00:03:33.510 --> 00:03:38.490
That's when I realized why he was mostly stealing from Maggie.

46
00:03:38.491 --> 00:03:41.871
All her stuff smells like cats!"

47
00:03:41.872 --> 00:03:48.260
Eleanor gasped. "I didn't know you had cats, Maggie!"

48
00:03:48.261 --> 00:03:53.750
"I have two kittens," Maggie said. "They're really cute."

49
00:03:53.751 --> 00:04:00.275
Ms. Wood picked up the saddle pad. "I owe you an apology, Maggie," she said.

50
00:04:00.276 --> 00:04:03.670
"I'm sorry I accused you of losing this.

51
00:04:03.671 --> 00:04:09.082
I guess you got some cat hair on it and that's why Spot took it."

52
00:04:09.083 --> 00:04:11.541
She noticed the halter.

53
00:04:11.542 --> 00:04:16.927
"Sometimes the barn cat knocks down the spare halters and sleeps on them."

54
00:04:16.928 --> 00:04:19.733
Maggie held up the second brush.

55
00:04:19.734 --> 00:04:22.975
"And I bet someone used this to brush the cat."

56
00:04:22.976 --> 00:04:26.028
"I'm sorry," Eleanor said.

57
00:04:26.029 --> 00:04:30.464
"I promise to watch Little Spot more closely from now on."

58
00:04:30.465 --> 00:04:33.302
"That's okay." Maggie shrugged.

59
00:04:33.303 --> 00:04:38.570
"It's just a good thing The Lemonade Detectives were here to solve the case."

60
00:04:38.571 --> 00:04:44.034
"The Lemonade Detectives?" Ms. Wood looked at Henry, Cole, and Maggie.

61
00:04:44.035 --> 00:04:46.441
"I've heard about you three!

62
00:04:46.442 --> 00:04:51.195
My neighbor hired you when he couldn't remember who'd borrowed his tennis racket.

63
00:04:51.196 --> 00:04:54.191
He said you tracked it down within an hour."

64
00:04:54.192 --> 00:04:58.856
Cole nodded. "That was us."

65
00:04:58.857 --> 00:05:01.742
Ms. Wood put a hand in her pocket.

66
00:05:01.743 --> 00:05:07.401
"Then I'd better pay your detective fee," she said. "Five dollars, right?"

67
00:05:07.402 --> 00:05:10.624
"You don't have to pay us," Henry said.

68
00:05:10.625 --> 00:05:14.353
"Maggie's the one who wanted us to solve this case."

69
00:05:14.354 --> 00:05:19.540
"I insist." Ms. Wood handed him a five-dollar bill.

70
00:05:19.541 --> 00:05:22.488
"You found several of my missing things.

71
00:05:22.489 --> 00:05:28.280
More importantly you proved that one of my favorite new students isn't careless."

72
00:05:28.281 --> 00:05:33.297
She smiled at Maggie. "That's worth at least five dollars, right?"

73
00:05:33.298 --> 00:05:38.939
"Definitely," Maggie agreed. "Henry and Cole saved the day.

74
00:05:38.940 --> 00:05:43.866
If they hadn't solved the case, I might have had to stop riding!"

75
00:05:43.867 --> 00:05:50.041
She shook her head and smiled. "And all because of a cat-loving dog!"

76
00:05:50.042 --> 00:05:54.997
Little Spot barked and wagged his tail. Everyone laughed.

77
00:05:54.998 --> 00:05:59.237
"Thanks," Henry said, taking the money from Ms. Wood.

78
00:05:59.238 --> 00:06:08.873
"I guess that's another case closed for The Lemonade Detectives!"
